deferred Recurrence.next_due_date


-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════
-- RESOLVED DECISIONS
-- ═════════════════════════════════════════════

-- resolved: Utility bills remain normal expenses, not a separate expense type.
-- resolved: Utility entry gets a specialized workflow to make manual entry easier.
-- resolved: One utility expense may contain multiple utility bill lines.
-- resolved: Utility kind and expense context are separate dimensions.
-- resolved: Expense context is reusable across all expense categories.
-- resolved: Expense context is stored at expense level for the first release; line items do not
--           have separate context overrides.
-- resolved: "Home electricity" is a template/shortcut label, not a category or subcategory.
-- resolved: Expense templates are tenant-shared, not personal/private, for the first release.
-- resolved: Recurring expenses create reminders and prefilled manual-entry drafts only for now.
-- resolved: Recurring reminders are in-app only for the first release; no email/push delivery.
-- resolved: Recurring/subscription-like examples include mobile, AI, hosting, and donations.
-- resolved: Mobile, internet, hosting, and AI tools default to the Subscriptions category.
-- resolved: Donations can be recurring without necessarily belonging to a Subscriptions category.
-- resolved: Utility workflow uses purchased_at / paid date only for first-release reporting;
--           billing period and due date are deferred.
-- resolved: Utility and recurring workflows apply to both web and mobile clients, with shared
--           domain rules and client-specific presentation only.


